---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Restaurant",
  name: "Nobu",
  servesCuisine: ["Japanese", "Japanese-Peruvian"],
  priceRange: "$$$$",
  telephone: "+1-702-785-6628",
  url: "https://www.caesars.com/caesars-palace/restaurants/nobu",
  address: {
    "@type": "PostalAddress",
    streetAddress: "3570 Las Vegas Blvd S",
    addressLocality: "Las Vegas",
    addressRegion: "NV",
    postalCode: "89109",
    addressCountry: "US",
  },
  description:
    "Nobu at Caesars Palace, Las Vegas — Nobu Matsuhisa's Japanese-Peruvian fine-dining restaurant inside the world's first Nobu Hotel.",
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Nobu Las Vegas Menu Guide (2026) — Prices, What to Order | Hotel Menu Guide"
  description="An independent guide to Nobu at Caesars Palace Las Vegas: official menu prices (black cod miso $49, omakase $250), hours, and visiting tips. Prices from the official Nobu menu, October 2026."
  path="/nobu-menu/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  ogImage="/images/nobu-dining.webp"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <img
      src="/images/nobu-dining.webp"
      alt="Illustration of a sleek modern Japanese restaurant with dark wood and warm lighting (illustrative, not the actual restaurant)"
      class="w-full h-64 sm:h-96 object-cover rounded-2xl mt-8"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />

    <p class="mt-8 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-gold-dark">
      Menu Guide · Las Vegas
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mt-2 leading-tight">
      Nobu — Menu Guide
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      The Caesars Palace outpost of Nobu Matsuhisa's global empire sits inside the
      <strong>world's first Nobu Hotel</strong> — opened in 2013 as a venture between
      Matsuhisa, Caesars Palace, Robert De Niro, and Meir Teper, in a David Rockwell-designed
      space. It was reported at opening as the world's largest Nobu restaurant, and it
      remains the <strong>only Nobu in the United States with teppan tables</strong>, where
      the teppanyaki omakase is cooked in front of you. OpenTable has named it an Icon in
      2024, 2025, and 2026. A note on stars: the previous Nobu location at the old Hard
      Rock held a Michelin star in the 2008–2009 Vegas guides, but the Caesars Palace
      location earned no star in the inaugural 2026 Michelin Guide Southwest. Below is our
      independent walkthrough with prices from the current official Nobu menu (fetched
      October 2026), plus what we'd order. Everything is written in our own words.
    </p>

    <!-- At a glance -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">At a glance</h2>
      <dl class="mt-4 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2 text-sm">
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Location</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">3570 Las Vegas Blvd S, Las Vegas, NV 89109 (inside Caesars Palace / Nobu Hotel)</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Chef</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Nobu Matsuhisa (founder); Jennifer Chow per OpenTable</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Cuisine</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Japanese / Japanese-Peruvian</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Price level</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Very expensive — signatures $35–$60; Japanese A5 wagyu $55/oz</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Reservations</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Recommended; bookable via OpenTable or +1 (702) 785-6628</dd></div>
        <div><dt class="font-semibold text-ink">Hours</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">Mon–Thu &amp; Sun 5:00–9:30 PM; Fri–Sat 4:30–10:00 PM (per OpenTable)</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-guide">
      <h2>Hours</h2>
      <p>
        Reported by OpenTable and Caesars.com: <strong>Monday–Thursday and Sunday,
        5:00–9:30 PM; Friday–Saturday, 4:30–10:00 PM</strong> (Caesars.com lists Friday–Saturday
        to 10:30 PM — confirm when booking). Dinner only.
      </p>

      <h2>Signatures &amp; official prices</h2>
      <p>
        Prices below are from the <strong>current official Nobu menu</strong> (noburestaurants.com,
        fetched October 2026):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Black Cod with Miso — $49</strong>: the signature dish, the one order that defines Nobu.</li>
        <li><strong>Yellowtail Jalapeño — $37</strong>; <strong>Rock Shrimp Tempura — $35</strong>; <strong>Toro Tartare with Caviar — $60</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Japanese A5 Wagyu — $55 per ounce</strong> (tataki, new style, tobanyaki, steak, or flambé).</li>
        <li><strong>Beef Tenderloin Yuzu Truffle Butter — $110</strong>; <strong>Lobster Wasabi Pepper — $150</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Brick Oven Hamachi Kama — $40</strong>; <strong>Nobu Tacos</strong> — wagyu $20/pc, lobster $18/pc (2-pc minimum).</li>
        <li><strong>Sushi</strong>: toro $25/pc, Japanese wagyu $25/pc, uni $22/pc; maki from $17 (spicy tuna) to $42 (lobster).</li>
        <li><strong>Teppanyaki Omakase — $250 per guest</strong>: multi-course, prepared on the teppan grills; the whole table must participate, and it's not available after 9 PM.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we'd order</h2>
      <p>If we had one meal here, this is how we'd play it:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Non-negotiable:</strong> the black cod with miso ($49) — the dish that built the brand.</li>
        <li><strong>The classics:</strong> yellowtail jalapeño ($37) and rock shrimp tempura ($35) — the Nobu canon.</li>
        <li><strong>The splurge:</strong> A5 wagyu by the ounce ($55/oz) — or the $250 teppanyaki omakase for the full theater.</li>
        <li><strong>Easy start:</strong> edamame ($10) or shishito peppers ($12) while you decide.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Planning your visit</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Book via OpenTable</strong> — it's an OpenTable Icon three years running (2024–2026), and prime slots go fast. Groups of 14+: (866) 733-5827.</li>
        <li><strong>Dress code:</strong> business casual.</li>
        <li><strong>Teppanyaki note:</strong> the $250 omakase requires the whole table to participate and isn't available after 9 PM — plan an earlier seating if that's your goal.</li>
        <li><strong>The vegetarian and "Caesars" omakase</strong> prices aren't published on the official menu — ask when you book.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Official links</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.caesars.com/caesars-palace/restaurants/nobu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official restaurant page — Caesars Palace</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.noburestaurants.com/lasvegascaesars/menus/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Official menu — noburestaurants.com</a> (current prices)</li>
        <li><a href="https://www.opentable.com/nobu-caesars-palace-las-vegas" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Reservations — OpenTable</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Price disclaimer -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border border-gold/40 bg-gold/10 p-5 text-sm text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <p class="font-semibold text-ink mb-1">About these prices</p>
      <p>
        All prices above are from the <strong>current official Nobu menu at
        noburestaurants.com, fetched October 2026</strong> — the most current source
        available. Menus and prices change frequently; always verify with the restaurant
        before visiting.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Related guides -->
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6 sm:p-8">
      <h2 class="!mt-0 font-display text-xl font-bold">More Las Vegas guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-sm">
        <li><a href="/best-hotel-restaurants-nevada/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">The best hotel restaurants in Nevada →</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guy-savoy-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Restaurant Guy Savoy at Caesars Palace</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— French fine dining in the same hotel</span></li>
        <li><a href="/joel-robuchon-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Joël Robuchon at MGM Grand</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— the Strip's other tasting-menu temple</span></li>
        <li><a href="/carbone-menu/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">Carbone at Aria</a> <span class="text-ink-soft">— Italian-American glamour</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-ink-soft">
      <a href="/" class="text-gold-dark font-semibold hover:underline">← Back to all guides</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
